  "rationale": "Blocking jumpHost:lateralMovement, backupHost:lateralMovement and printServer:lateralMovement makes the target unreachable. (1) mailArchive needs jumpHost, so it is cut. (2) dbReplica needs jumpHost, backupHost or printServer, so it is cut. (3) secretsManager is an AND step that needs printServer, so it is cut, and with it codeRepo. (4) localAdmin is an AND step that needs jumpHost, so it is cut; shareMount's parents (secretsManager, localAdmin, backupHost) are then all cut. Two blocks are not enough because there are three attack paths that share no blockable step: wifiGuest->kerberoast->jumpHost->mailArchive->target; internet->tokenCache->backupHost->shareMount->target; wifiGuest->sshKey and ciRunner->dbLogin->printServer->dbReplica->target. Each path needs its own block, so the minimum is 3."
